    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file, even though `frai-gate init --ci` (direct call) works correctly.\n\n## Root Cause\nIn the frai CLI's gate command handler, commander.js wasn't properly passing the variadic arguments (especially the `--ci` flag) to the action handler. The `args` parameter in the action callback was not receiving the command-line arguments as expected.\n\n## Solution\nI fixed the gate command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Remove reliance on commander.js passing the variadic arguments\n2. Manually extract all arguments from `process.argv` after the 'gate' command\n3. Pass these arguments directly to the frai-gate subprocess\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Rebuilt the frai CLI with `pnpm --filter frai build`  \n\u2705 Tested the fix in a clean directory - running `frai gate init --ci` now successfully creates:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe workflow file contains the correct GitHub Actions configuration for running the RAI Gate check on every pull request.",
